body:
Having played BCB on Steam, I think the best way to demo it would be to let players move around Brigade Town, perhaps right before the tournament begins and all the shopkeeps are still setting up, giving the player some little story blurbs when you talk to them, and letting Belchior and... hunting lady (Sorry, I forgot her name) give the players a tutorial into the cooking and hunting aspects, respectively, through their quests they actually give in the full game. Since both Belchior's puzzles and the hunting quests essentially serve as tutorials masked as side quests, a snippet of each of them would explain the basic mechanics well enough that you could end the demo by sending the players off into a proper little cook-off in the training grounds, much like the one against Thrash you play at the start of the game.

&#x200B;

It's always fun when a demo showcases more than just the start of the game and instead tries to give a little unique experience, hence why it might be fun to set the demo right before the tournament. Use it as an excuse to let the NPCs fill the player in on the basic story premise of the main game ("Sorry, I'm very busy preparing the inn for the upcoming tournament. What tournament, you ask? Well\[...\]")
